host/bin/sysdb/_objs/bgen.cc_binary/sysdb/bgen/src/bgen_lex.d -iquote . -iquote bazel-out/host/genfiles -iquote external/bazel_tools -iquote bazel-out/host/genfiles/external/bazel_tools -I bazel-out/host/bin/sysdb/_virtual_includes/backend_headers -I bazel-out/host/bin/linux/os/_virtual_includes/headers -I bazel-out/host/bin/thirdparty/opensource/sdk/_virtual_includes/x86_64_headers -I bazel-out/host/bin/thirdparty/opensource/sdk/_virtual_includes/x86_64_headers_bits_headers -I bazel-out/host/bin/thirdparty/opensource/sdk/_virtual_includes/x86_64_linux_headers -isystem external/bazel_tools/tools/cpp/gcc3 -c -fno-builtin -g '-DCPP_CMD=gcc.c4.7.0-p1 -D DISABLE_API_VERSION_MACRO -D__BASE_OS_LINUX__ -D__x86_64__ -E %s -x c %s -o %s' -DSIGNAL_H_MISSING_SIGEVENT_STRUCT -Ibgen/src -O2 -fno-inline-functions-called-once -fno-strict-aliasing -fno-omit-frame-pointer -fno-reorder-functions -c bazel-out/host/bin/sysdb/bgen/src/bgen_lex.c -o bazel-out/host/bin/sysdb/_objs/bgen.cc_binary/sysdb/bgen/src/bgen_lex.o).\r\nIn file included from bazel-out/host/bin/thirdparty/opensource/sdk/_virtual_includes/x86_64_headers/lnx/stdio.h:74:0,\r\n                 from bazel-out/host/bin/linux/os/_virtual_includes/headers/xros_wrapper.h:40,\r\n                 from bazel-out/host/bin/linux/os/_virtual_includes/headers/stdio.h:14,\r\n                 from bazel-out/host/bin/sysdb/bgen/src/bgen_lex.c.temp:12:\r\n/usr/include/libio.h:307:3: error: unknown type name 'size_t'\r\n/usr/include/libio.h:311:67: error: 'size_t' undeclared here (not in a function)\r\n/usr/include/libio.h:339:62: error: expected declaration specifiers or '...' before 'size_t'\r\n/usr/include/libio.h:348:6: error: expected declaration specifiers or '...' before 'size_t'\r\n/usr/include/libio.h:470:19: error: expected '=', ',', ';', 'asm' or '__attribute__' before '_IO_sgetn'\r\n\r\nMy question:\r\n1. Why there is \"-g0\"?  It is commented out in the host tool's CROSSTOOL file and where is \"-g0 -MD -MF\" coming from? why it is building *.d?\r\n\r\nThe /usr/include in \"cxx_builtin_include_directory\" in the host CROSSTOOL has \"size_t\" defined.  \r\n\r\n2. Why the error is traced back to bazel-out/host/bin/sysdb/bgen/src/bgen_lex.c.temp?  This is intermediary output of a target that produces bgen_lex.c.  I don't include it in the struct's depset of that target's rule skylark implementation output.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/344123532/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"indrgun","id":2126004,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMjYwMDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2126004?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/indrgun","html_url":"https://github.com/indrgun","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/indrgun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/indrgun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/indrgun/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/indrgun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/indrgun/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/indrgun/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/indrgun/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/indrgun/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/indrgun/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/344687619","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/3507#issuecomment-344687619","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/3507","id":344687619,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM0NDY4NzYxOQ==","user":{"login":"hlopko","id":814566,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxNDU2Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/814566?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hlopko","html_url":"https://github.com/hlopko","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hlopko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hlopko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hlopko/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hlopko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hlopko/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hlopko/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hlopko/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hlopko/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hlopko/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-11-15T18:40:17Z","updated_at":"2017-11-15T18:40:17Z","body":"Uff too many questions to respond to without inline responses. I'll try.\r\n\r\nI don't know what external/bazel_tools/tools/cpp/gcc3 is but without it google breaks. I didn't have time to investigate more.\r\n\r\nI don't know if it causes unknown type name 'size_t'.\r\n\r\nBazel patches legacy crosstools by https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/blob/275ae45b1228bdd0f912c4fbd634b29ba4180383/src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/rules/cpp/CppActionConfigs.java I think that's where the flags come from. Unless you have a custom crosstool that defines feature named 'no_legacy_features'. Let me know if you do.\r\n\r\nC++ rules unconditionally generate .d file (last time I checked it was not trivial to turn it off) and use the information to speed up the build (by not rebuilding targets that don't really use the changed dependency).\r\n\r\nI've no idea why the error is tracked back to bazel-out/host/bin/sysdb/bgen/src/bgen_lex.c.temp, you can investigate by running bazel with `--subcommands`, then observing the commands bazel generates, `cd`-ing into the sandbox, and running the command manually. 